   "answer": "**Result: Michaelis-Menten fit of beta-galactosidase ONPG initial rates**\n\nI re-read the source table and the saved fit table. The values below match those logs.\n\nSteps:\n1. I read the rate table. It has 10 rows, one rate for each ONPG concentration. It has no replicates and no inhibitor.\n2. I ran the enzyme kinetics fit with the Michaelis-Menten model on the onpg_mM and rate_mM_per_min columns. No rows were dropped (n = 10).\n3. I read Vmax and Km with their 95% confidence intervals from the fit.\n\nEstimates (nonlinear least squares, 10 rates):\n- **Vmax = 0.1841 mM/min** (95% CI 0.1697 to 0.1985 mM/min; SE 0.00625 mM/min)\n- **Km = 2.479 mM** (95% CI 1.772 to 3.187 mM; SE 0.307 mM)\n\nWhat I found:\n- The curve follows the low and middle substrate points closely.\n- The highest substrate points do not fall on one side of the curve. At 20 mM the rate is 0.152 mM/min. At 30 mM the rate is 0.181 mM/min. The 20 mM rate lies below the curve and the 30 mM rate lies above it.\n- The Vmax estimate depends on these two points. The harness data check on the first file read flagged the 20 mM and 30 mM substrate values as extreme values (rows 10 and 11). It flagged the substrate column only, not the rates. I kept both points.\n- The Lineweaver-Burk plot is a view only. I did not use it for Km or Vmax.\n\nWhat is uncertain:\n- There are no replicate wells, so the fit has no error estimate for each rate. Each rate has equal weight, which is the tool default.\n- I cannot verify the drc version from the logs. Please check the installed drc version before you report the numbers.\n- The scatter at high substrate can come from substrate limits or from assay error. The data cannot show which.\n\nWhat waits for you:\n- Confirm that the 20 mM and 30 mM rates are valid. If they are not, I can refit without them.\n- Confirm the drc version that the lab uses.\n- Confirm that Michaelis-Menten is the model you want. Inhibition models do not apply, because there is no inhibitor.\n\nFiles: the fit table and plot are in the fit_enzyme_kinetics-1 folder of the session.\n\nSettings used, from the decision record: Enzyme kinetic model: michaelis-menten.",
