   "dir": "/Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/cooley2020-splitluc-zprime/run1/home/sessions/20261009-001300-fd5f",
   "answer": "## Result: Z' for ten plates at two volumes\n\nI calculated the mean, SD and Z' of the positive and negative wells for each plate and volume. All 20 groups have Z' of 0.5 or more. The lowest Z' is 0.522 (plate 2, 20 µL).\n\n### Steps\n1. I read the plate file. It has 240 wells: 5 positive and 5 negative wells for each volume on each plate, plus 2 blank wells for each volume on each plate.\n2. I made one group for each plate and volume (for example 1_10ul).\n3. I ran the plate control tool on the 20 groups. It used percent activity normalization, with Z' from the mean and SD. It excluded no wells and did not subtract the blank.\n4. I ran a script on the 40 blank wells to get their range.\n\n### Table (signal in the units of the file; n = 5 positive and 5 negative wells in each row)\n\n| Plate | Volume (µL) | Positive mean | Positive SD | Negative mean | Negative SD | Z' |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 10 | 2471.2 | 268.1 | 416.8 | 46.0 | 0.541 |\n| 1 | 20 | 1337.4 | 73.4 | 167.4 | 29.4 | 0.736 |\n| 2 | 10 | 2252.8 | 211.3 | 383.8 | 31.6 | 0.610 |\n| 2 | 20 | 1200.4 | 143.8 | 158.0 | 22.3 | 0.522 |\n| 3 | 10 | 3134.0 | 204.6 | 500.2 | 34.6 | 0.728 |\n| 3 | 20 | 1728.8 | 101.4 | 156.8 | 31.6 | 0.746 |\n| 4 | 10 | 2540.6 | 153.0 | 435.6 | 36.2 | 0.730 |\n| 4 | 20 | 1326.2 | 55.1 | 181.8 | 26.4 | 0.786 |\n| 5 | 10 | 2826.8 | 205.5 | 464.6 | 58.8 | 0.664 |\n| 5 | 20 | 1689.6 | 52.1 | 111.0 | 25.5 | 0.852 |\n| 6 | 10 | 2686.6 | 221.2 | 438.2 | 54.7 | 0.632 |\n| 6 | 20 | 1530.4 | 149.7 | 148.6 | 14.8 | 0.643 |\n| 7 | 10 | 2214.8 | 106.9 | 429.2 | 32.0 | 0.767 |\n| 7 | 20 | 1378.8 | 108.1 | 158.8 | 25.8 | 0.671 |\n| 8 | 10 | 2453.6 | 111.9 | 391.2 | 65.8 | 0.742 |\n| 8 | 20 | 1369.2 | 107.8 | 156.2 | 19.6 | 0.685 |\n| 9 | 10 | 2189.6 | 185.1 | 372.4 | 44.5 | 0.621 |\n| 9 | 20 | 1209.4 | 57.4 | 139.2 | 13.8 | 0.800 |\n| 10 | 10 | 2249.0 | 135.5 | 368.8 | 38.9 | 0.722 |\n| 10 | 20 | 1233.8 | 79.7 | 123.4 | 20.9 | 0.728 |\n\nZ' formula used by the tool: Z' = 1 − 3 × (SD positive + SD negative) / |mean positive − mean negative|.\n\n### Summary of Z' (calculated from the table values)\n- All 20 groups: mean Z' 0.696; lowest 0.522 (plate 2, 20 µL); highest 0.852 (plate 5, 20 µL).\n- 10 µL (10 groups): mean Z' 0.676; range 0.541 to 0.767.\n- 20 µL (10 groups): mean Z' 0.717; range 0.522 to 0.852.\n\n### Blank wells (script output, not used in Z')\n- 40 blank wells (2 per volume per plate).\n- Blank mean 151.8, SD 33.1.\n- Lowest blank 94.0 (plate 5, well P5-I8). Highest blank 240.0 (plate 2, well P2-D8).\n\n### What I found\n- Z' is 0.5 or more in all 20 groups. I used 0.5 as the limit for an excellent screening assay (Zhang et al. 1999).\n- The positive signal is higher at 10 µL (means from 2189.6 to 3134.0) than at 20 µL (means from 1200.4 to 1728.8). The negative signal is similar at both volumes.\n\n### What is uncertain\n- The blank wells are not subtracted from the signal. Blank subtraction changes the mean and Z' values.\n- Each Z' uses 5 positive and 5 negative wells, so each Z' value has wide uncertainty.\n- The tool did not give a lab limit for Z'. I used the 0.5 limit from the literature.\n- The data file check with inspect_data failed. I read the file directly, and the file had no missing values.\n\n### What waits for you\n- Do you want blank subtraction before the Z' calculation? I can run it.\n- Is 0.5 the Z' limit that your lab uses?\n- Do any wells need to be excluded as outliers? I excluded none.\n\nStep results that the answer does not mention, from the record:\n- n1 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/cooley2020-splitluc-zprime/run1/home/sessions/20261009-001300-fd5f/work and wrote 1 new file(s) to /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2026-10-09/claude_claude-haiku-5-5/cooley2020-splitluc-zprime/run1/home/sessions/20261009-001300-fd5f/work.\n- n4 run_script: The script ran in /Volumes/T7/guided-analysis/tools/bench-runs/2